WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.760
What is Pi?

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.680
Let's assume, we are asked to draw a circle of radius three centimeters.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.200
So we draw a circle like this.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.760
The length of this red thing will be the perimeter.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.620
And we have a special name for the perimeter of a circle.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.400
It's called the circumference.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.440
This length will be the circumference.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.760
This length will measure 18.85 centimeters.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.220
The next thing we need to find out is the diameter of the circle.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.520
The diameter of a circle is twice its radius.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.920
Hence, the diameter will be 2 multiplied by 3,

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.840
which equals 6 centimeters.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.480
Now we've been asked to draw a circle of radius four centimeters.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.800
It will be slightly bigger than the previous one.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.840
This red boundary will be the circumference.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.780
This time too we measure the circumference.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.920
For this circle we get the circumference as,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.600
25.1 Centimeters.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:11.240
And the Diameter will be twice its radius, which equals 8 centimeters.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:14.100
We looked at two different cases here.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.760
One circle with three as the radius,

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.440
and another with four as its radius.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:25.160
In both cases we calculated the circumference and the diameter.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.700
Let's zoom out and find the ratio

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.220
of circumference by diameter in each case.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.920
If we calculate the value of circumference by diameter in the first case,

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.640
we will approximately get it as 3.14.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.680
And guess what! In the second case too

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:48.320
we get the value of circumference by diameter as approximately 3.14.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.480
No matter what circle you look at

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.080
the value of circumference by diameter

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:57.360
will always be approximately equal to 3.14.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.700
This value is Pi.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:03.880
Remember, both these values are approximations.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.680
Now let's zoom out and deduce a formula for the circumference.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.980
As the circumference by diameter equals Pi ,

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.800
we can say that the circumference of a circle

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.660
equals Pi multiplied by the Diameter.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.860
If we call the diameter 'D' then the formula can be written as

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.260
'Pi multiplied by D'.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.120
Which can also be written as 'Pi multiplied by 2R'.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:32.440
Because the diameter is twice the radius.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.040
So the circumference of a circle is written as 2 Pi R.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.560
All we did was write this product a bit differently.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.440
This is a very important formula, as it gives us the value of the circumference

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.660
even if you just have the radius of the circle.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.020
There's another important thing about this special Constant Pi.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.140
We get the same value if we divide 22 by 7.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.480
So the value of Pi approximately equals

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.880
3.14

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.080
or 22 by 7.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.800
But why do we use this symbol for Pi?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.920
What is this symbol?

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:15.940
Pi, is actually the 16th letter of the Greek alphabet.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.220
But the question still remains why the 16th letter?

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.580
We just saw that Pi has got something to do with the perimeter.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:27.500
or the circumference of the circle.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.720
Let's use Google Translate

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:33.200
to see the Greek equivalent of perimeter .

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.820
As we can see the first letter of the Greek word is Pi.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.540
Let's try a couple of more words related to perimeter.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.620
How about periphery?

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.040
The first letter is still Pi.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.860
Hmm. Okay, let's try circumference.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.120
The first letter as all of us can see is still pi.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:58.980
That's probably why this symbol was used to denote Pi.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:03:59.760
Anyway,

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.840
don't forget the important point. Pi is the circumference of the circle,

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.560
divided by its diameter.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:12.020
So it is the ratio of the circumference to the diameter.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.580
Based on the formula if the diameter of the circle is 1 unit.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.580
Then its circumference will be Pi units.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.140
If we have a circle like this

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.700
with diameter equal to 1 unit,

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:29.040
then the length of this boundary will be Pi,

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:33.120
or approximately 3.14 units.

